        "calls": 1,
        "title": "Freebuff chat header displays ended session Freebucks refund receipt",
        "summary": "The Freebuff chat header now renders a receipt line for the Freebucks refund from the most recently ended session, passing `lastRefund` and `refundPending` from the session store through the component tree. A new `freebucksRefundLine` helper in `cli/src/utils/freebucks.ts` formats the receipt, distinguishing pending settlements, zero refunds, and positive amounts to clarify that the refund reflects unspent charge rather than unused time. The session store's `refreshRefund` now sets `lastRefund` to null when a settled receipt omits an amount, preventing an abandoned settlement from being displayed as a zero refund.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "In `cli/src/utils/freebucks.ts`, the new `freebucksRefundLine` function formats refund receipts for the UI, returning distinct strings for pending, zero, and positive amounts. In `cli/src/components/freebuff-chat-header.tsx`, this line is rendered in the panel when `lastRefund` or `refundPending` is set.",
        "userVisible": true,
        "confidence": "medium",
